{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019793-is-withstanding-static-or-reflexive","id":1019793,"title":"Is withstanding static or reflexive?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T08:45:55-08:00","id":1019793,"title":"Is withstanding static or reflexive?","content":"I'm curious if withstanding is something that can be buffed by other splats. Is withstanding a supernal spell a static action that is set using the current values of Endurance, Resolve, or other trait, or is it reflexive and thus can be modified by increasing the relevant withstand trait?<br /> <br /> For example, a Moros necromancer attempts to cast the equivalent of a Paralyze Undead spell on a Requiem vampire. Can the vampire increase their withstand rating by using physical intensity to pump up their Endurance?<br /> <br /> This brings a second question to the topic. Is such a reflexive increasing of the withstand trait automatic, or does it require knowledge that Endurance or another trait is used to fend of the magic? Does the victim have to &quot;see it coming&quot; and know what trait to increase, or does the body (or soul) just handle it instinctively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:52:03-08:00","id":1019795,"title":"","content":"You can increase your Withstand by 2 by spending a WP. You have to know you should be increasing Withstand though, it's not Reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T13:33:41-08:00","id":1019948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019793-is-withstanding-static-or-reflexive#post1019793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if withstanding is something that can be buffed by other splats. Is withstanding a supernal spell a static action that is set using the current values of Endurance, Resolve, or other trait, or is it reflexive and thus can be modified by increasing the relevant withstand trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no such thing as a &quot;static&quot; action.<br /> <br /> Withstand ratings are based of the target's Resistance traits, which can be boosted by any standard means of doing so. The important thing though is that the boost adds to your Trait rating or says it improves your Resistance. A +2 dice to Stamina rolls will have no effect on Withstand. +3 dice to Stamina rolls or +2 to Resistance will increase Stamina based Withstand by 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can the vampire increase their withstand rating by using physical intensity to pump up their Endurance? </div> </div> </div>If they are aware of the spell being cast, yes, since Physical Intensity says that the boosts apply to Resistance traits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is such a reflexive increasing of the withstand trait automatic, or does it require knowledge that Endurance or another trait is used to fend of the magic? Does the victim have to &quot;see it coming&quot; and know what trait to increase, or does the body (or soul) just handle it instinctively? </div> </div> </div>The magic rules do not require you to know the specifics of the spell to boost your Withstand, only that you be aware of magic being cast on you. Interpret how the character knows which trait to boost however you feel works best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019793-is-withstanding-static-or-reflexive?p=1019795#post1019795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can increase your Withstand by 2 by spending a WP. You have to know you should be increasing Withstand though, it's not Reflexive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is Reflexive. Reflexive actions can have qualifiers on their use (such as needing to be aware of the need to use them). Something is Reflexive as an action if it doesn't take up your action to do it. Withstanding is Reflexive. Spending WP is Reflexive. Using Physical Intensity is Reflexive. Nothing indicates that this somehow turns into an Instant action if you do it.<br /> <br /> If you're being attacks, applying your Defense is a Reflexive action (though Dodging is not). But you need to know the attack is coming to do so (and then to spend WP on it, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T19:49:01-08:00","id":1020135,"title":"","content":"Remember that you also may decide to not apply your Withstand. So by default, you Withstand, and you can make a conscious decision of not Withstanding. This can be relevant if, for example, your Mage is rocking a bilion Withstand and for whatever reason can't react to friendly spell being cast on them. A classic example is &quot;Mage falls unconcious and is dying, their companions can't heal them because WARDS AND SIGNS 9999999999).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:05:53-08:00","id":1020265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019793-is-withstanding-static-or-reflexive?p=1020135#post1020135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A classic example is &quot;Mage falls unconcious and is dying, their companions can't heal them because WARDS AND SIGNS 9999999999).</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that you mention that. My group had a similar situation where the designated healer got knocked out, but no one could find him because he had 24 hour duration invisibility spell on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}